, normally dry\narroyos and slot canyons are possible Sunday through Monday.\n\nPlease follow the evolving forecast, especially if your plans\nincluding recreating or commuting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-10T05:59:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 100559 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1159 PM MDT Fri Oct 9 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - A pattern change arrives through the weekend bringing another round of tropical moisture to the region. - Rainfall totals of 1-2 inches and locally higher are possible over the eastern Utah mountains and the San Juans. Moderate to heavy rainfall rates are ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-10T08:45:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Remnant moisture from Tropical Storm Rachel will filter into the region today. Wetting rains are expected to develop across the region by early this evening, with some isolated showers and thunderstorms expected by this morning. Strong winds and the potential for severe thunderstorms arrive Sunday as this system moves into the local area. Flash flooding, hail, and strong winds are c","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=